# goLLums
.claude

# Git worktrees created from INSIDE the repo.
#
# The house convention puts worktrees in `CourtHive/.worktrees/`, a SIBLING of the repos, where
# nothing needs ignoring. But `git worktree add .worktrees/<name>` resolves relative to the CURRENT
# directory, so running it from inside the repo silently creates one in the working tree instead —
# a slip that differs from the correct command only by where you happen to be standing.
#
# The result is a permanent `?? .worktrees/` in every `git status`, for every session in the repo,
# plus the risk of committing it as an embedded gitlink. Git does not recurse into a nested repo, so
# it is one line of noise rather than thousands of files — but it is one line that never goes away
# and that everyone has to learn to ignore.
#
# NOT a gate problem, and that was measured rather than assumed: vitest (`include: src/**`), eslint
# (`eslint src`), prettier (`format:check` on `src/**`) and tsc (`include` inherited from
# tsconfig.base.json) are all anchored at `src/`, so none of them would ever walk it. Factory was
# already fixed for the old `.claude/worktrees` case by #4604.
.worktrees/

